; All view ops
(constructor LogicalIndexMapApply (LogicalTensor IndexMap Shape) LogicalTensor)

; The relations of rewrite.egg, declared with the constructor so every op's
; rewrites can name them whatever the splice order.
; The identity-map fold.
(relation index-map-identity-suffix (IntExprList Shape))
; COMPOSITION. An index map is a lambda: the apply's out shape binds the
; coordinates, the entries are the body, the tag is the parent shape it
; reads. A view of a view reads its operand through the composite of the two
; maps: first the outer (the view's coordinates into the intermediate box),
; then the inner (the intermediate box into the parent). The composite is
; computed, as a literal: the inner's entries substituted under the outer map
; (`int-subst-of`, one row per entry), over the inner's tag.
; `index-map-compose-demand inner outer` asks for it, the entry walk builds
; it, and `index-map-composed inner outer composite` publishes it.
(relation index-map-compose-demand (IndexMap IndexMap))
(relation index-map-composed (IndexMap IndexMap IndexMap))
(relation composed-entries-demand (IntExprList IndexMap))
(relation composed-entries (IntExprList IndexMap IntExprList))
; VIEWED BOUNDS: the value bounds of a tensor restricted to what a view of
; it reads, keyed by the view's map, derived ON DEMAND (`viewed-bounds-demand`)
; and only as facts: no view of the tensor is minted. A view of a select
; demands its condition's viewed bounds; the demand descends the
; condition's pointwise chain (comparison, cast, sum, a view) to its
; sources (an iota: the bounds of its expression substituted under the map;
; anything with value bounds: those, a view reads a subset); the comparison
; is decided where its operands' viewed bounds separate; a select whose
; condition is decided over the view is, through that view, the view of
; the decided branch (select/rewrite.egg). This is how a slice of a
; concatenation (a select on a mask over clamped padding views) reaches the
; operand it reads, without distributing the view into the condition.
(relation viewed-bounds-demand (LogicalTensor IndexMap))
(function viewed-lower-bound-of (LogicalTensor IndexMap) BigInt :merge (max old new))
(function viewed-upper-bound-of (LogicalTensor IndexMap) BigInt :merge (min old new))
